<!--
  The one record. AAO_Extract reads "Default" by name and fails loudly if it is missing,
  rather than falling back to a constant, because a fallback constant is exactly the
  hardcoding this type exists to prevent.

  Charter version is 1.0.0 because this is the first charter that reads anything. The 0.1.0
  that came before it was the fixture: proposals authored by hand and staged by artifact
  hash. Those two must never share a version string, or candidate rows from a run that read
  a transcript become indistinguishable from rows a human wrote.

  AAO_Anthropic_Beta__c is deliberately absent rather than present and empty. An omitted
  field on a custom metadata record is null, and null is the normal case here.

  Extraction is 1.1.0 as of session 8: the FALSE bar was tightened so that absence of a
  confirmation can no longer be read as a denial. The version moved because the instructions
  moved, which is the whole point of versioning a charter. Candidate rows written at 1.0.0
  were produced by a charter that did not say that.

  The blind reader is a second charter with its own version. It is the check that decides
  whether cited spans actually establish an element, and its no overrides claimed coverage.
-->
<CustomMetadata xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
    <label>Default</label>
    <protected>false</protected>
    <values>
        <field>AAO_Active__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:boolean">true</value>
    </values>
    <values>
        <field>AAO_Charter_Version__c</field>
        <value xsi:type="xsd:string">1.1.0</value>
    </values>
    <values>
